The two levers that carry a spatial shape are narrowed with the model:
\code{GREEN_H2}, whose \code{for.each} names every province, and \code{CO2_CAP}, whose cap
is a per-province allowance times the province count and so is rescaled by
the count kept. \code{CT_CO2} and \code{EARLY_RET} have no province dimension.

\code{layout} chooses which of the four pictures the model is drawn on. The
corridor network is the SAME on all four -- fourteen corridors frozen in
\code{data-raw/topia_links.R}, not derived from any one layout -- so a layout
changes the map and nothing the model solves.
